A '''Slayer Weapon''' is a weapon tied to a [[Slayer]], either unlocked through that Slayer's leveling rewards or built to deal increased damage against its mob type. Slayer Weapons are the main way to progress a Slayer track, because the majority of them multiply damage against the specific mobs a quest requires. Every Slayer has its own weapon line that grows in power as the player levels it.

== Overview ==
Most Slayer Weapons share common abilities against the Slayer's corresponding [[Mob Type|mob type]]:
* Grants an additive {{Stat|Damage}} multiplier.
* Grants {{Stat|Combat Wisdom}}, increasing {{Skl|Combat|XP}} from that mob type. 
* Reduce damage taken from the mob type.

Some also carry a utility ability like clearing the {{Mob|Tarantula Broodfather}}'s {{item|Cobweb}}s or vanquishing the {{Mob|Riftstalker Bloodfiend}} below {{HP|20%}}.

Due to the fact that the bonus is tied to a specific mob type, a Slayer Weapon is usually far stronger than a generic sword of the same rarity inside its own Slayer, and much weaker outside it. 

A few weapons from Slayers sit outside the main damage line. These are sidegrades, utility tools, or weapons that share the same source but serve a different purpose, such as the {{Item|Reaper Scythe}}, {{Item|Sinseeker Scythe}}, {{Item|Edible Mace}}, or {{Item|Steak Stake}}.

